{
  "info": {
    "name": "Film 5 - live minimum password length",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Film 5: the minimum password length as a live decision on a configuration ladder - a security_settings row (live) over a property (restart) over the code default (rebuild). Run 0.x once (register, verify with the token from Mailpit, authenticate), then 1-7 in order. GET /admin/settings/password reports the WHOLE policy in force, every rule under its key; POST /admin/settings/password/min-length is the one admin write, behind a step-up that the pre-request script buys afresh each time."
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "admin",
      "value": "admin@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "StrongPassword1!"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "verifyToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "minLength",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Register admin",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/register",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"email\":\"{{admin}}\",\"password\":\"{{adminPassword}}\"}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "0. Verify email (token from Mailpit :8025)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/verify-email",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"token\":\"{{verifyToken}}\"}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "0. Authenticate (stores token)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().accessToken);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/authenticate",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"email\":\"{{admin}}\",\"password\":\"{{adminPassword}}\"}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "1. GET password policy in force (ladder report, every rule under its key)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/settings/password",
        "description": "The whole password policy in force: every rule under its key, each with the value, the level that answered (live (database) > restart (properties/env) > rebuild (default)) and what was refused on the way with the gate's reason. The film follows security.password.policy.min.length; the other four rules climb the same ladder, so a row written at psql under any of the five keys is in force within one snapshot TTL, endpoint or no endpoint."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 for an ADMIN', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const policy = pm.response.json();",
              "const keys = [\"security.password.policy.min.length\", \"security.password.policy.special.chars\", \"security.password.policy.requires.uppercase\", \"security.password.policy.requires.lowercase\", \"security.password.policy.requires.digit\"];",
              "pm.test('every rule of the policy is reported under its key', () => keys.forEach(k => pm.expect(policy, k).to.have.property(k)));",
              "pm.test('each rule carries value, source and rejected', () => keys.forEach(k => {",
              "  pm.expect(policy[k]).to.have.all.keys('value', 'source', 'rejected');",
              "  pm.expect(policy[k].rejected).to.be.an('array');",
              "}));",
              "const length = policy['security.password.policy.min.length'];",
              "console.log('min length in force:', length.value, 'from', length.source, 'refused on the way:', JSON.stringify(length.rejected));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('minLength', String(length.value));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Step-up admin-settings",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/account/step-up",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"action\":\"admin-settings\",\"password\":\"{{adminPassword}}\"}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('elevated for admin-settings (password re-proven, no factors enrolled)', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ELEVATED');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. POST min-length = 10 [auto step-up]",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/settings/password/min-length",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"value\":10}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// elevation is consumed by ONE admin write - buy a fresh one right before this request",
              "pm.sendRequest({",
              "  url: pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') + '/account/step-up',",
              "  method: 'POST',",
              "  header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + pm.collectionVariables.get('token') },",
              "  body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({ action: 'admin-settings', password: pm.collectionVariables.get('adminPassword') }) }",
              "}, (err, res) => { if (err || res.code !== 200) console.warn('step-up failed', err || res.json()); });"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('ACCEPTED with the value now in force', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ status: 'ACCEPTED', value: 10 });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. POST min-length = 3 (refused) [auto step-up]",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/settings/password/min-length",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"value\":3}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// elevation is consumed by ONE admin write - buy a fresh one right before this request",
              "pm.sendRequest({",
              "  url: pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') + '/account/step-up',",
              "  method: 'POST',",
              "  header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + pm.collectionVariables.get('token') },",
              "  body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({ action: 'admin-settings', password: pm.collectionVariables.get('adminPassword') }) }",
              "}, (err, res) => { if (err || res.code !== 200) console.warn('step-up failed', err || res.json()); });"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('REFUSED at the door with the gate\\'s reason, nothing changes', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('REFUSED');",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().reason).to.include('at least 5');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Register user - 9 chars (422 when min is 10)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/register",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"email\":\"newcomer@example.com\",\"password\":\"Nine1!aaa\"}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('422 naming the minimum in force', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(422);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().passwordErrors).to.deep.include({ MIN_LENGTH_NOT_MET: 10 });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Register user - 5 chars (passes when min is 5)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/register",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"email\":\"short@example.com\",\"password\":\"Ab1!x\"}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 when the default 5 is in force', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Step-up with an action outside the catalogue (400 UNKNOWN_ACTION)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/account/step-up",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"action\":\"some-unknown-action\",\"password\":\"{{adminPassword}}\"}"
        },
        "description": "Sensitive actions are a catalogue (StepUpAction): each one carries the name on the wire, the key its requirement is configured under and the requirement the code ships. A name outside the catalogue is refused outright - no elevation is minted for something nobody would ever consume."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('400 UNKNOWN_ACTION', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('UNKNOWN_ACTION');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
